<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">People's Secretariat</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1917–1918</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The People's Secretariat was the government of the Bolshevik-led Ukrainian People's Republic of Soviets, formed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kharkiv">Kharkiv</a> in December 1917 as a rival to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-rada">Central Rada</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kyiv</a>. Its members included <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yevgenia-bosch">Yevhenia Bosh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mykola-skrypnyk">Mykola Skrypnyk</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volodymyr-zatonsky">Volodymyr Zatonsky</a>. It depended on Red Guards from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> and was dissolved in 1918 after the German and Austro-Hungarian advance into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/peoples-secretariat.jpg" alt="People's Secretariat" width="320" height="357" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: UnknownUnknown , · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emblem_of_the_Ukrainian_Soviet_Socialist_Republic_(1949%E2%80%931991),_Emblem_of_Ukraine_(1991%E2%80%931992).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
